From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mason Morris <masonmorris8@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:01:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Give up on lifecycle answers a stopped stream never sends

A stream that stopped after a device error runs no callback, and the
render thread lives in that callback, so suspend, resume and close
waited forever for an answer that never came, and so did the
embedder's promises.

Each now waits at most 2 s, as setSinkId already does. Without an
answer, suspend marks the context suspended and leaves the stream
alone, close marks it closed and closes the stream, and resume
returns with the context as it was.
